set-bg: img/map_2.jpg
new-page: true

> *"Universal and direct suffrage is the only means which in the long run of itself corrects the mistakes to which its momentary wrong use may lead. It is that spear which heals the wounds itself has made. It is impossible in the long run with universal and direct suffrage that the elected body should be any other than the exact and true likeness of the people which has elected it. The people must therefore at all times regard universal and direct suffrage as its indispensable political weapon, as the most fundamental and important of its demands."*

 - Ferdinand Lassalle, *The Working Man's Programme*, 1862

This is a work of alternate-history fiction set in the Federal Republic of Germany. While it draws upon real political institutions, parties, public figures and historical events, its scenarios, events and dialogue are fictionalized. Any divergence from actual events is intentional and part of the game's fictional setting.

This game is a work of satire and alternate-history fiction. It features real political parties and public figures, but all alternate-history scenarios, events, dialogue and decisions are invented and did not happen. Characters' statements in these scenarios are not real quotes and do not reflect the actual views, conduct or intentions of the people depicted. The game is intended for entertainment and education and is not political advice or campaign material.

